data.content:
## What Changed

The `Microsoft.AspNetCore.OpenApi` 10.0 package upgrades the underlying library from **Microsoft.OpenApi v1** to **v2**, which targets **OpenAPI 3.1**. Here are the breaking changes affecting your code:

### 1. `OpenApiString` / `OpenApiAny` types removed
The `Microsoft.OpenApi.Any` namespace is gone. Examples are now `System.Text.Json.Nodes.JsonNode`:

```csharp
// Before
using Microsoft.OpenApi.Any;
param.Schema.Example = new OpenApiString("1.0");

// After
using System.Text.Json.Nodes;
param.Schema.Example = JsonValue.Create("1.0");
```

### 2. `schema.Nullable` removed
OpenAPI 3.1 uses JSON Schema's type array instead of a `nullable` flag. Use the `JsonSchemaType.Null` flag:

```csharp
// Before
property.Value.Nullable = false;

// After  (to make nullable, OR in the flag; to clear it, AND it out)
property.Value.Type &= ~JsonSchemaType.Null;
```

You'll need `using Microsoft.OpenApi.Models;` (for `JsonSchemaType`).

### 3. `OpenApiSecurityRequirement` is no longer a dictionary
It no longer extends `Dictionary<OpenApiSecurityScheme, IList<string>>`. Use the `Schemes` property:

```csharp
// Before
new OpenApiSecurityRequirement
{
    [oAuthScheme] = scopes
};

// After
new OpenApiSecurityRequirement
{
    Schemes = { [oAuthScheme] = scopes }
};
```

### 4. `OpenApiReference.Type` → `ReferenceType` renamed

`ReferenceType` values were renamed (e.g., `ReferenceType.SecurityScheme` is now a string-based reference on `OpenApiReference`).

---

### Full corrected code

```csharp
using System.Text.Json.Nodes;
using Microsoft.OpenApi.Models;

options.AddOperationTransformer((operation, context, ct) =>
{
    var param = operation.Parameters.FirstOrDefault(p => p.Name == "api-version");
    if (param is not null)
    {
        param.Schema.Example = JsonValue.Create("1.0");
    }

    operation.Responses.TryAdd("401", new OpenApiResponse { Description = "Unauthorized" });

    var oAuthScheme = new OpenApiSecurityScheme
    {
        Reference = new OpenApiReference { Type = ReferenceType.SecurityScheme, Id = "oauth2" }
    };
    operation.Security = new List<OpenApiSecurityRequirement>
    {
        new()
        {
            Schemes = { [oAuthScheme] = scopes }
        }
    };

    return Task.CompletedTask;
});

options.AddSchemaTransformer((schema, context, ct) =>
{
    if (schema.Properties is not null)
    {
        foreach (var property in schema.Properties)
        {
            if (schema.Required?.Contains(property.Key) != true)
                property.Value.Type &= ~JsonSchemaType.Null;
        }
    }
    return Task.CompletedTask;
});
```

**Summary of removals:**
| .NET 9 (OpenApi v1) | .NET 10 (OpenApi v2) |
|---|---|
| `using Microsoft.OpenApi.Any` | `using System.Text.Json.Nodes` |
| `new OpenApiString("…")` | `JsonValue.Create("…")` |
| `schema.Nullable = false` | `schema.Type &= ~JsonSchemaType.Null` |
| `new() { [scheme] = scopes }` | `new() { Schemes = { [scheme] = scopes } }` |
